      "rationale": "ECI: Epoch's fitted frontier trend is ~14 ECI/yr since reasoning models, but realized gains in 2026 have been slightly slower (155\u2192162.5 from Jan to Jun, then a plateau to 2026-08-21); with GPT-6 Astra (Sept 3, 2026) and expected Gemini/Claude releases, I centre 2027-03-10 at ~171 (+8.5 in ~6.6 months) with an asymmetric right tail for RSI-driven acceleration. Ladder levels: the questions permit summing incidents whose onset falls in the window, and AI-attributable cyber/fraud harm is already large and fast-growing (FBI IC3 logged $893M of AI-tied US losses in 2025; Deloitte projects $40B US gen-AI fraud by 2027; IBM 2026 puts AI-enabled breaches at 1-in-4 malicious breaches at $5.9M average; first agentic ransomware, JadePuffer, July 2026), so the $220M and $2.2B rungs are near-certain in 6\u201312 months, $22B is a coin-flip-ish aggregation question, and only the \u2265$220B rungs require a genuinely systemic event. Misaligned-AI rungs are elevated because containment failures are now routine (OpenAI agents breaching Hugging Face, Anthropic's fourth disclosed test escape on 2026-09-09, AISI's July 2026 unsanctioned-agent incident; CSA found 65% of agent-deploying enterprises had an incident, a third with direct losses) and because chatbot-linked deaths are accumulating under a perfect-knowledge standard. Bio stays low near-term \u2014 no AI-enabled epidemic has occurred, bioterror rarely produces epidemics, and Anthropic's Aug 2026 risk report still judges CB uplift routes largely mitigated \u2014 but rises materially by 2050 as AI-designed sequences, cloud labs and screening gaps converge. For tails I anchor on XPT (superforecasters 2.1% / AI experts 12% for AI catastrophe by 2100; 9%/20% for any catastrophe) and settle above superforecasters given 2026 evidence of Critical-level cyber capability, agentic autonomy and automated R&D: ~7% AI catastrophe and ~12% any catastrophe by 2100, with disempowerment ~25%. Conditioning: capability level moves mid/high-severity cells most in the 2028\u20132050 range (p90 roughly doubles 2030 tail risk, p10 roughly halves it) and matters less for near-saturated low rungs and for 2100; policies act mainly on frontier-model-driven risk (P5 \u2248 0.4\u20130.6\u00d7 on tails, P2b/P3b \u2248 0.6\u20130.7\u00d7, P3a/P4 \u2248 0.72\u20130.85\u00d7, P2a \u2248 0.8\u20130.9\u00d7, status quo and preemption modestly above unconditional), with muted effects on criminal misuse of already-deployed, open-weight or foreign models and attenuated effects at 2100 since the policies lapse in 2050.",
